cff-version: 1.2.0
message: "If you use this dataset or code, please cite it as below."
title: "QRShield v2: A Benchmark for Visual Tamper Detection in QR Codes Beyond the Training Distribution"
type: dataset
version: "2.0"
date-released: 2026-11-13
authors:
  - family-names: Hafeez
    given-names: Memona
    orcid: "https://orcid.org/0009-0007-4258-2386"
repository-code: "https://github.com/Memona-hafeez/QRShield_v2"
license: MIT
abstract: >-
  QRShield v2 is a synthetic benchmark of 66,083 images for visual tamper
  detection in QR codes, with five tamper families, styled and logo-bearing
  benign codes as hard negatives, and a camera-degradation layer. It comes with
  a leakage-free evaluation protocol (base-code group split, leave-one-family-out
  testing, validation-only thresholding) and baselines that measure
  generalisation beyond the training distribution. The code is released under
  the MIT license; the dataset and report under CC BY 4.0.
keywords:
  - QR code security
  - quishing
  - tamper detection
  - distribution shift
  - benchmark
  - adversarial robustness
